cordis-harness
==============

This project composes selected, unchanged DeepSeek Harness plugins with the
Rust-backed cordis-verus compatibility runtime. It is an independent project,
not an official DeepSeek release or an endorsement by the upstream authors.

Original application and plugin code is licensed under LICENSE (MIT).
DeepSeek Harness source: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
The exact revision, tree and archive digest are recorded in sources.lock.json.
Its MIT license is preserved in third-party/DeepSeek-Harness.LICENSE. Bundled
upstream sources retain their legal comments and dist/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.

cordis-verus source: https://github.com/validation-engineering/cordis-verus
The current runtime is an unpublished, development-validated source snapshot.
sources.lock.json records its clean source commit, content fingerprint and
package digests. Restoring that commit recovers source; native artifacts and
local validation evidence must be prepared separately.
Its license and notices are in third-party/Cordis-Verus.LICENSE and
third-party/Cordis-Verus.NOTICE, and are also included in the installed packages.
The packages include upstream Cordis MIT notices and native build provenance.

Zod and eventsource-parser are included in the official plugin bundle. Their
MIT license texts are in third-party/Zod.LICENSE and
third-party/eventsource-parser.LICENSE. esbuild is used only at build time;
its MIT text is in third-party/esbuild.LICENSE. Exact dependency versions and
registry integrity hashes are recorded in package-lock.json.

No paper PDF or model credentials are distributed. Development evidence does
not establish complete Harness compatibility, full paper refinement, release
acceptance, or support for untested native platforms.
